# d45 CI source diagnosis and measurement draft

HEAD inspected: d45c3610a586fab926a98a8656bb337792a38b6c. CI run36349836006, native x64 ASan job108706257669. Exact-head artifact downloaded by integrated_perf_fixture agent under adjacent ci-d45/native-x64-ASan-Debug. Menu log fails TestLargeMenuPaintsOnlyVisibleRowsWithCachedOffsets: End-to-visible latency remains bounded. MenuAccessibility passes. The intentional ASan Foundation probe is not the failure.

The failing fixture has4096 ordinary rows and a240-DIP viewport. Open is bounded at5s, End-to-visible at1s. It asserts successful last-row selection/positive scroll before failing latency. Old timing emits occur after the assertion, so the failure did not retain a numeric elapsed value.

Source trace: WM_KEYDOWN End -> RouteMenuKeyboardEvent -> EnsureItemVisible (cached offsets) -> InvalidatePopup -> SynchronizeMenuAccessibility. Synchronization loops4096 retained semantic children, clips/sets their rectangles and updates logical focus. A changed focus calls SetFocusControl once; its snapshot publication excludes the geometry-refresh else-if. The inspected End path therefore has no duplicated geometry snapshot from the newly added else-if. Snapshot construction does full navigation and point-hit traversals plus focus-path search. Those inspected flat-menu passes are linear; no quadratic builder established. Ordinary semantic node materialization does add full snapshot construction/string ownership and RTTI work at4096 rows that the original plain-menu path avoided. This is a plausible cost, not yet an isolated measured root cause. PumpMessages and debug-state copying are also inside the measured bound.

No speculative product optimization or threshold change is proposed. large-end-witness.patch exposes the exact existing fixture in MenuAccessibility, keeps4096rows and all bounds, and emits flushed JSON before assertions: open duration; End synchronous dispatch; message pump; full debug-state query; total; last-row condition; painted-row count. Root applied/formatted that patch. large-focus-invariants.patch is incremental: the nonactivating lane requires the existing ScopedWindowActivationBlocker and verifies foreground/native focus at open/navigation/teardown; the native Menu lane retains activation behavior. The established test.ps1 runner passes --no-activate for MenuAccessibility, and DxUiTests.cpp installs the thread CBT blocker before suite execution.

All evidence and drafts here are external. No repository edit/build/native execution by this agent. Both patches passed read-only apply checks when frozen. Root should collect matching baseline/candidate fixture results before choosing an algorithmic fix; existing native Menu remains an independent gate.
